"""The slimmer parser prompt (PROMPT-RULES-DIET): exact-text edits that bring the list-free parser text from
129,651 chars to under 90,000 with the same behaviour.

Applies to the text `chatbot_lookup_edits` produces (it ends in the `== LOOKUP LISTS ==` line). Rounds r01 to
r05 were measured one by one on the crew eval ledger (documentation/plans/chatbot/PLAN-prompt-rules-diet-26oct.md);
the edits here are those round files, in order. The policy block region is not touched. Edits apply IN ORDER and
each anchor must occur exactly once in the text as it stands when its turn comes (a later round anchors on text an
earlier round wrote); any miss or double returns None and nothing partial is published. `replace_line` anchors
are the sha256 of one whole line, so a line that quotes a real name is never quoted here. Pure and stdlib-only
(plus the lookup module), so a migration can import it.
"""
