    Edit('replace', 'Every signal word below is DECISIVE. If the current message contains one — in ANY\nlanguage, paraphrase, or misspelling, matched by MEANING not spelling — SET that\ndomain and intent, OVERRIDING the previous turn\'s domain. This applies to EVERY term\nlisted, not only the obvious ones: "ETA" sets incoming, "dimension" sets\nmaster_products, "selling price" sets promotion, just as decisively as the clearer\ncases. The previous domain is NOT a tiebreaker against a decisive term — the term\nwins. A product carried from the previous turn stays as the scoping entity when the\ndomain switches (drop an attachment_type entity when switching to master_products).\nOnly when NO decisive term is present AND the domain is genuinely ambiguous → set\ndomain_hint and intent_hint to null.', 'Every signal word below is DECISIVE: in the current message (ANY language, paraphrase or misspelling, by MEANING not spelling) it SETS that domain and intent, OVERRIDING the previous turn\'s domain, for EVERY term listed ("ETA" sets incoming, "dimension" sets master_products, "selling price" sets promotion). A product carried from the previous turn stays the scoping entity when the domain switches (drop an attachment_type entity when switching to master_products). Only with NO decisive term AND a genuinely ambiguous domain → domain_hint and intent_hint null.'),
