    Edit('replace', '  FULL TIMELINE — emit the SINGLE sentinel ["__all__"] and nothing else when the user wants the\n  WHOLE picture rather than one date: "container status of X", "what\'s the status of container X",\n  "full status", "all the dates", "the timeline", "everything on this shipment".\n  It returns every checkpoint that IS recorded. It deliberately does NOT report the ones that are\n  not, and does NOT mention fields the contact may not see — the customer named no field, so\n  silence about a missing or restricted one is the correct answer. Naming a field explicitly is\n  what turns those messages back on.\n  A bare "where is my shipment" / "when is it coming" asks only for the ETA — leave\n  requested_attributes = [] and let the default answer stand.', '  FULL TIMELINE — the SINGLE sentinel ["__all__"] and nothing else when the user wants the WHOLE picture rather than one date: "what\'s the status of container X", "full status", "all the dates", "the timeline", "everything on this shipment".\n  A bare "where is my shipment" / "when is it coming" asks only for the ETA: requested_attributes [].'),
