    # lever 5: arrow form, domain / intent pair as in DECISIVE DOMAIN TERMS.
    Edit('replace', '"list price", "normal price", "RRP" or a bare "price" of a product → domain_hint master_products, intent_hint check_product; "selling price", "promo price", "promotion price", "discount price", "offer" → domain_hint promotion, intent_hint check_promotion. DECISIVE over the previous domain, also when "list price" appeared inside earlier promotion results.', '"list price", "normal price", "RRP" or a bare "price" of a product → master_products / check_product; "selling price", "promo price", "promotion price", "discount price", "offer" → promotion / check_promotion (domain_hint / intent_hint). DECISIVE over the previous domain, also when "list price" appeared inside earlier promotion results.'),
    # lever 4: arrow form; every escalate word kept.
    Edit('replace', '"is_affirmative" (top level): true for a bare affirmative or any agreement in any language; false for a bare decline; null otherwise (the message carries its own content).\nESCALATE-WORD: when the previous response OFFERED an escalation ("Would you like me to escalate ...") and the current message is the escalate word itself, in any language, case or short form, with or without filler ("ESCALATE", "escalate", "escalate please", "pls escalate", "ok escalate", "escalate this", "eskalasi", "升级", "escalate to the team"), set "is_affirmative": true, exactly like "yes" (it is ALSO request_for_help, see MESSAGE TYPE).', '"is_affirmative" (top level): true for a bare affirmative or any agreement in any language; false for a bare decline; null when the message carries its own content.\nESCALATE-WORD: the previous response OFFERED an escalation ("Would you like me to escalate ...") and the message is the escalate word itself, any language, case or short form, with or without filler ("ESCALATE", "escalate", "escalate please", "pls escalate", "ok escalate", "escalate this", "eskalasi", "升级", "escalate to the team") -> "is_affirmative": true, like "yes" (and request_for_help, MESSAGE TYPE).'),
    # lever 4: terse; "WEAKEST signal ... whatever the previous response showed" folded into "al
    Edit('replace', 'Read the current message against what your previous response did, which decides how to read a short reply: (A) it ASKED something (a question, a choice between options, or a proposal: "would you like me to escalate?", "which access level?"); or (B) it DELIVERED an answer or results and asked for nothing further.\n\nA "Current subject:" line in the user block (domains, customers, products, document, status, date window) is CONTEXT for reading a short message: emit only what the CURRENT message says.\n  - ONLY a domain ("promotion", "stock", "incoming", "PO", "outstanding"): a DOMAIN SWITCH about the SAME subject, domain_hint = the new domain, no entities of its own; entity_op your call ("reuse" when it names no value).\n  - A value of its own ("for SRTWC286 only", "this month") REFINES the subject: emit that value and nothing else.\n  - The subject\'s DOMAINS are the WEAKEST signal: a domain or status word in the CURRENT message always wins, however badly spelled and whatever the previous response showed ("oustaning quantity for CB88SS" under a stock listing is an ORDER ask about CB88SS, see ORDER_STATUS FILTER). The SUBJECT continues, the DOMAIN does not.\n  - A number written as a WORD is a position: "one", "two", "three", "eight", "the eighth one", the Malay "satu", "dua", "lapan" and the Chinese numerals go to reference_positions exactly as "8" does (see POSITIONAL REFERENCES).', 'Read the message against what your previous response did, which decides how to read a short reply: (A) it ASKED something (a question, a choice, a proposal: "would you like me to escalate?", "which access level?"); (B) it DELIVERED an answer and asked nothing.\n\nA "Current subject:" line in the user block (domains, customers, products, document, status, date window) is CONTEXT only; emit what the CURRENT message says:\n  - ONLY a domain ("promotion", "stock", "incoming", "PO", "outstanding") -> DOMAIN SWITCH on the SAME subject: domain_hint = that domain, no entities of its own, entity_op your call ("reuse" when no value).\n  - a value of its own ("for SRTWC286 only", "this month") REFINES the subject: that value only.\n  - a domain or status word in the CURRENT message beats the subject\'s domains, however misspelt, even under a stock listing: the SUBJECT continues, the DOMAIN does not.\n  - a number written as a WORD is a position like "8": "one", "two", "three", "eight", "the eighth one", Malay "satu", "dua", "lapan", the Chinese numerals -> reference_positions.'),
    # lever 4+5: the nine example rows (padded columns, each repeating -> true / false with its 
    Edit('replace', 'domain_in_message is true when THIS message itself carries a DOMAIN or STATUS word -\nstock, incoming, ETA, delivery, order, outstanding, DO, SO, PO, purchase cost, promo,\nprice, spec, photo, catalogue, certificate, installation guide, forms, shipment, GRN - in any language.\nIt is false when the message only names entities, a date window or a place, and leans\non the previous turn for what is being asked. It is about the WORDS of this message,\nnever about domain_hint (which is carried forward when the message names no domain).\n  - "outstanding DO for 7445"      -> true  ("outstanding", "DO")\n  - "how about delivery?"           -> true  ("delivery", and it names no entity)\n  - "check stock srtwc286"          -> true  ("stock")\n  - "for 7445"                      -> false (an entity and nothing else)\n  - "7445 only"                     -> false\n  - "in august only"                -> false (a date window)\n  - "for <customer name> only"               -> false (a customer)\n  - "at <warehouse code>"                        -> false (a place)\n  - "1" / "all" / "yes"          -> false', 'domain_in_message = true when THIS message itself carries a DOMAIN or STATUS word (stock, incoming, ETA, delivery, order, outstanding, DO, SO, PO, purchase cost, promo, price, spec, photo, catalogue, certificate, installation guide, forms, shipment, GRN, any language); false when it only names entities, a date window or a place. About the WORDS of this message, never domain_hint (which carries forward).\n  - true: "outstanding DO for 7445", "how about delivery?" (no entity)\n  - false: "for 7445", "in august only", "for <customer name> only", "at <warehouse code>", "1" / "all" / "yes"'),
    # class 1: the three examples ("ETA" sets incoming, "dimension" sets master_products, "selli
    Edit('replace', 'Every signal word below is DECISIVE: in the current message (ANY language, paraphrase or misspelling, by MEANING not spelling) it SETS that domain and intent, OVERRIDING the previous turn\'s domain, for EVERY term listed ("ETA" sets incoming, "dimension" sets master_products, "selling price" sets promotion). A product carried from the previous turn stays the scoping entity when the domain switches (drop an attachment_type entity when switching to master_products). Only with NO decisive term AND a genuinely ambiguous domain → domain_hint and intent_hint null.', "Every signal word below is DECISIVE (ANY language, paraphrase or misspelling, by MEANING): it SETS that domain and intent, OVERRIDING the previous turn's domain; a product carried from the previous turn stays the scoping entity (drop an attachment_type entity when switching to master_products). NO decisive term AND a genuinely ambiguous domain → domain_hint and intent_hint null."),
    # class 1: "the standing price, NOT a promotion price" is the PRICE TERMINOLOGY mapping, kep
    Edit('replace', '    → product, product code, description; product details, dimension, size, measurement, width/height/depth, "how big", weight, material, colour, finish; LIST / normal / RRP price or a bare "price" of a product (the standing price, NOT a promotion price; see PRICE TERMINOLOGY); asking about discontinue of item.', '    → product, product code, description; product details, dimension, size, measurement, width/height/depth, "how big", weight, material, colour, finish; LIST / normal / RRP price or a bare "price" of a product (PRICE TERMINOLOGY); asking about discontinue of item.'),
    # lever 4: terse; warning line verbatim; every term and example kept.
    Edit('replace', '    → product catalogue, warranty / warranty policy / warranty poster, price tag template, brand guarantee document, container status list / container status report / container status sheet / shipping schedule; also "katalog", "senarai status kontena". Only a document-class word plus a brand or company name ("Catalog Sorento", "Mocha warranty", "katalog Sorento") is get_resource_attachment with the attachment entity, never promotion.\n      ⚠ THE DOCUMENT NOUN DECIDES, NOT THE PHRASE "container status".\n      "container status LIST / REPORT / SHEET / FILE / EXCEL", "shipping schedule" = the document itself → THIS domain. Bare "container status" asks about a SHIPMENT, not for the file: "what is the container status of SRTWC286-SH-NEW", "container status for TCNU1851000" → domain_hint incoming, requested_attributes ["__all__"].', '    → product catalogue, warranty / warranty policy / warranty poster, price tag template, brand guarantee document, container status list / container status report / container status sheet / shipping schedule, "katalog", "senarai status kontena"; a document-class word plus only a brand or company name ("Catalog Sorento", "Mocha warranty", "katalog Sorento") is this domain with the attachment entity, never promotion.\n      ⚠ THE DOCUMENT NOUN DECIDES, NOT THE PHRASE "container status".\n      "container status LIST / REPORT / SHEET / FILE / EXCEL", "shipping schedule" = the file → THIS domain; bare "container status" asks about a SHIPMENT ("what is the container status of SRTWC286-SH-NEW", "container status for TCNU1851000") → domain_hint incoming, requested_attributes ["__all__"].'),
    # lever 4: "for one or more customers", "what that customer ORDERED from us", "(an order)" a
    Edit('replace', '    → GOODS GOING OUT to a CUSTOMER: an existing customer order, delivery order (DO), its status or delivery, delivery status, delivery date, "delivery order", "DO", "hantar" about a customer. A CUSTOMER NAME anywhere in a delivery/DO/order question is a "customer" entity, NEVER inbound_shipment; "delivery" as fulfilment of a customer order belongs HERE, never incoming. A customer\'s "outstanding list", "pending list", "outstanding orders", "delivery list" or "belum hantar" (undelivered ORDERS for one or more customers, not stock balance) is ALSO order / check_order with order_status set, NEVER inventory/check_stock.\n      ALSO DECISIVE: a customer TAKING / BUYING a product from us ("X have take Y", "X have sales Y", "did X take/buy Y", "X took Y", "X bought Y", "X ada ambil Y"), what that customer ORDERED from us → order / check_order, order_status null (all their orders), BOTH entities {hint:"customer"} for X and {hint:"product"} for Y, requested_attributes ["quantity"]. "sales" / "have sales" here is a SALE MADE (an order), NOT a sales promotion. A stock or promotion/price term in the same message wins over this rule: "does X have stock Y" → inventory; "X have sales promotion / promo price / selling price Y" → promotion.', '    → GOODS GOING OUT to a CUSTOMER: an existing customer order, delivery order (DO), its status or delivery, delivery status, delivery date, "delivery order", "DO", "hantar" about a customer (fulfilment "delivery" is HERE, never incoming; a CUSTOMER NAME in it is a "customer" entity, NEVER inbound_shipment); also a customer\'s "outstanding list", "pending list", "outstanding orders", "delivery list", "belum hantar" (undelivered ORDERS, not stock balance), with order_status set, NEVER inventory/check_stock.\n      ALSO DECISIVE, a customer TAKING / BUYING from us ("X have take Y", "X have sales Y", "did X take/buy Y", "X took Y", "X bought Y", "X ada ambil Y") → order / check_order, order_status null (all their orders), BOTH entities {hint:"customer"} X and {hint:"product"} Y, requested_attributes ["quantity"] ("sales" / "have sales" = a SALE MADE, NOT a sales promotion); a stock or promotion/price term in the same message wins ("does X have stock Y" → inventory; "X have sales promotion / promo price / selling price Y" → promotion).'),
    # lever 4: "INTO the warehouse", "of an inbound container" and "NOT product_attachment" (the
    Edit('replace', '    → GOODS COMING IN from a SUPPLIER INTO the warehouse: ETA, estimated arrival, "when will it arrive", incoming shipment, container number. The CODE in an incoming ask is the product; only a 4-letter + 7-digit token (e.g. CMAU4318062) is a container.\n      ALSO DECISIVE, the SHIPMENT CLEARANCE checkpoints of an inbound container: CIDB inspection / CIDB approval / "cleared CIDB", gate pass, warehouse arrival, collection informed, collection / "can I collect", loading, ETC, ETD / departure / sailed, liner / shipping line, China forwarder, Malaysia or local forwarder, consignee, warehouse, free days, container location, stacked, COA permit.\n      ⚠ "cleared CIDB" / "CIDB cert" on a SHIPMENT or container is THIS domain, NOT product_attachment; a CIDB/SPAN/SIRIM certificate DOCUMENT for a product is product_attachment.', '    → GOODS COMING IN from a SUPPLIER: ETA, estimated arrival, "when will it arrive", incoming shipment, container number; the CODE in such an ask is the product, only a 4-letter + 7-digit token (e.g. CMAU4318062) is a container.\n      ALSO DECISIVE, the SHIPMENT CLEARANCE checkpoints: CIDB inspection / CIDB approval / "cleared CIDB", gate pass, warehouse arrival, collection informed, collection / "can I collect", loading, ETC, ETD / departure / sailed, liner / shipping line, China forwarder, Malaysia or local forwarder, consignee, warehouse, free days, container location, stacked, COA permit.\n      ⚠ "cleared CIDB" / "CIDB cert" on a SHIPMENT or container is THIS domain; a CIDB/SPAN/SIRIM certificate DOCUMENT for a product is product_attachment.'),
    # lever 4: terse; every example phrase and the three NOT-ideate exits kept.
    Edit('replace', '    → the user PROPOSES something that does not exist yet (an idea, a suggestion, a feature request, an improvement, a wish for how the system/product/process should behave): "I have an idea", "it would be great if…", "can you add…", "you should let us…", "cadangan", "saya ada idea", "why don\'t we…", "suggestion: …". NOT ideate: asking for existing data (stock, price, ETA, order status, a document), which stays in its own domain; a complaint about existing behaviour (stays portal_link/complaint); asking for a human (stays request_for_help).\n\nNo decisive term and the previous turn\'s domain still fits (a continuation like "and its price?") → keep the previous domain.', '    → a PROPOSAL of something that does not exist yet (idea, suggestion, feature request, improvement, a wish for how things should behave): "I have an idea", "it would be great if…", "can you add…", "you should let us…", "cadangan", "saya ada idea", "why don\'t we…", "suggestion: …". NOT ideate: existing data (stock, price, ETA, order status, a document; its own domain), a complaint about existing behaviour (portal_link/complaint), a human (request_for_help).\n\nNo decisive term and the previous domain still fits ("and its price?") → keep it.'),
    # lever 4: terse; every condition, value and example kept.
    Edit('replace', 'A message that is ONLY an entity value (a product code, a customer/company name, an order/SPO/DO number) with no purpose word is the SAME question about a NEW value: "check stock for A" then "B" means check the stock for B.\n  - Previous turn had a business domain: CONTINUE it (its domain_hint and intent_hint, message_type "business_query", entity_op "replace_combine") and ALWAYS emit the value as an entity with current_message true and its proper hint, never entities [].\n  - No previous business domain: leave domain_hint null; a bare value never implies a domain.\n  - A decisive term in the current message ("spec", "list price", "dimension", "promo", "ETA") still moves the domain normally.\n  - Not for a bare reply that ANSWERS what the assistant just offered (a numbered did-you-mean / picker / access-level list, or an escalation offer): that is a pick (see REFERENCE TARGET and COMPANY-NAME REPLY), and a bare ordinal like "2" is a pick, never a product code. A value NOT among the offered choices (a company the offer did not list, a code the list does not carry) is no answer: it re-scopes the question, and this rule applies.', 'ONLY an entity value (a product code, a customer/company name, an order/SPO/DO number), no purpose word = the SAME question about a NEW value ("check stock for A", then "B" = stock for B):\n  - previous business domain → CONTINUE it (its domain_hint and intent_hint, message_type "business_query", entity_op "replace_combine"), the value ALWAYS an entity (current_message true, proper hint), never entities [].\n  - none → domain_hint null (a bare value never implies a domain).\n  - a decisive term ("spec", "list price", "dimension", "promo", "ETA") still moves the domain.\n  - not a bare reply ANSWERING an offer just made (a numbered did-you-mean / picker / access-level list, an escalation offer): a pick (REFERENCE TARGET, COMPANY-NAME REPLY); a bare ordinal like "2" is a pick, never a product code. A value NOT among the offered choices (a company the offer did not list, a code the list does not carry) re-scopes the question: this rule applies.'),
    # lever 4: bullets folded; "not a new lookup value or code" restates entity_op "reuse". Ever
    Edit('replace', 'When the previous turn\'s domain was "ideate", the assistant is COLLECTING an idea and asked a follow-up. A short plain answer ("it\'s for the operations team", "so we stop missing SLAs", "yes", "the warehouse guys") CONTINUES the idea: domain_hint "ideate", intent_hint "submit_idea", message_type "business_query".\n  - A team/department named AS THE ANSWER to who the idea is for is NOT request_for_help; that needs an actual ask for a person/agent to take over ("get me a human", "let me talk to someone").\n  - A DECISIVE term from another domain (stock/ETA/price) still switches domain normally.\n\nA standalone "DO", "D.O.", "d/o", or "delivery order" (any language) asks to VIEW a DELIVERY ORDER (domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order", message_type "business_query"), never the verb "do" or casual chatter; with a prior order / SPO code or order number in context, entity_op "reuse", not a new lookup value or code.', 'Previous domain "ideate" (COLLECTING an idea, a follow-up asked): a short plain answer ("it\'s for the operations team", "so we stop missing SLAs", "yes", "the warehouse guys") CONTINUES it: domain_hint "ideate", intent_hint "submit_idea", message_type "business_query". A team/department named AS THE ANSWER to who it is for is NOT request_for_help (that needs an actual ask for a person/agent to take over: "get me a human", "let me talk to someone"); a DECISIVE term of another domain (stock/ETA/price) still switches.\n\nA standalone "DO", "D.O.", "d/o", or "delivery order" (any language) = VIEW a DELIVERY ORDER (domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order", message_type "business_query"), never the verb "do" or chatter; a prior order / SPO code or order number in context -> entity_op "reuse".'),
