    # lever 4: the broken two-sentence wrap ("A date window does NOT make it specific / scope_in
    Edit('replace', 'scope_intent captures whether the user wants to BROADEN to everything or narrow to a\nspecific subset. Judge by meaning, in any language or phrasing:\n  - "broaden" → the user asks for ALL / everything / the whole list with no narrowing\n    value. A date window does NOT make it specific\n    scope_intent means the user broadened EVERY axis at once. Widening ONE axis is not that —\n    see BROADEN AXIS below, and set broaden_axis instead of scope_intent.\n  - "specific" → the user names a narrowing value — they want that subset.\n  - null → neither is clear.', 'scope_intent, by meaning in any language:\n  - "broaden" → ALL / everything / the whole list with no narrowing value, EVERY axis at once (a date window does NOT make it specific); widening ONE axis is broaden_axis instead (BROADEN AXIS).\n  - "specific" → the user names a narrowing value.\n  - null → neither is clear.'),
    # lever 4: rule 1 absorbs the separate "request_for_help outranks business_query, clarificat
    Edit('replace', 'message_type and is_affirmative are INDEPENDENT: a leading "no" sets is_affirmative=false but does NOT by itself force casual. Classify message_type from the current message alone (the previous response, an offer or a delivered answer, is context only), by this test, in order:\n1. The user asks for a human/agent/staff OR a specific team/department to help/handle it, OR asks to ESCALATE ("escalate", "please escalate", "escalate this", "escalate to <team>", "eskalasi", "升级": the escalate verb in any language/case/short form, the word alone is enough, with or without a topic, offered before or not) → message_type = request_for_help, even when the message also declines a prior offer (is_affirmative=false then). Fill intent_hint/domain_hint/entities from any topic, else null/[]. "share", "send", "give me", "provide", "pls share" aimed at DATA (a list, report, status, the outstanding list) is a DATA request (business_query), NOT request_for_help: that needs an explicit ask for a PERSON (human/agent/staff) or a named team/department.', 'message_type from the current message alone (the previous response, offer or answer, is context only), by this test in order; INDEPENDENT of is_affirmative (a leading "no" sets is_affirmative=false, never by itself casual):\n1. A human/agent/staff OR a specific team/department asked to help/handle it, OR ESCALATE ("escalate", "please escalate", "escalate this", "escalate to <team>", "eskalasi", "升级": that verb in any language/case/short form, alone enough, with or without a topic, offered before or not) → request_for_help, even when it also declines a prior offer (is_affirmative=false then) or mentions a product or order; intent_hint/domain_hint/entities from any topic, else null/[]. "share", "send", "give me", "provide", "pls share" aimed at DATA (a list, report, status, the outstanding list) is a DATA request (business_query): request_for_help needs an explicit ask for a PERSON (human/agent/staff) or a named team/department.'),
    # lever 4: telegraphic rules; the outranks line moved into rule 1; same values.
    Edit('replace', '2. If you have set BOTH a non-null intent_hint AND a non-null domain_hint → message_type MUST be "business_query".\n3. domain_hint null because the domain is genuinely undetermined, or the user asks what can you do / what is your capability → message_type = "clarification" (a bare entity value continuing the previous turn\'s domain is business_query, see BARE ENTITY CONTINUATION).\n4. Otherwise: "casual" or "unknown" (cannot classify).\n\n"clarification" is YOUR uncertainty about what the user wants, NOT the user\'s: a message where the USER doubts or questions your previous answer, or asks you to re-check/re-confirm, is "business_query", whatever its questioning or doubting tone.\n\n"request_for_help" outranks business_query, clarification and casual, even when the message also mentions a product or order.\n\nIf more than one type fits, choose the most specific.', '2. BOTH a non-null intent_hint AND a non-null domain_hint → "business_query".\n3. domain_hint null because the domain is genuinely undetermined, or "what can you do" / "what is your capability" → "clarification" (a bare entity value continuing the previous domain is business_query).\n4. Otherwise "casual" or "unknown".\n\n"clarification" is YOUR uncertainty, NOT the user\'s: a user doubting or questioning your previous answer, or asking to re-check/re-confirm, is "business_query". More than one type fits -> the most specific.'),
    # lever 4: terse.
    Edit('replace', 'A kind of attachment the user names OR IMPLIES (by meaning, any language, even with no attachment noun) → a SEPARATE entity {hint:"attachment_type"} beside the product entity, canonical_code = the taxonomy value of the kind meant, never the customer\'s own word. "how does it look", "looks like", "show me", "see it" imply a photo.', 'An attachment kind the user names OR IMPLIES (by meaning, any language, no attachment noun needed) → a SEPARATE {hint:"attachment_type"} entity beside the product, canonical_code = the taxonomy value of the kind meant, never the customer\'s word; "how does it look", "looks like", "show me", "see it" imply a photo.'),
    # lever 4: list inline; same seven values.
    Edit('replace', 'access_levels = the level(s) the user SELECTS or names IN THE CURRENT MESSAGE, ONLY from:\n["Sorento Dealer","Mocha Dealer","Mocha Office","Cabana Dealer","Cabana Office","End User","Sorento Office"]\nNo other strings, never an entity, never carried forward or inferred from previous turns; none named → [].\n  - brand + "dealer" / "office" → that brand\'s level ("sorento" + "dealer" → "Sorento Dealer", "mocha" + "office" → "Mocha Office", the same for cabana); "dealer" / "office" with no brand → all three ("Sorento Dealer","Mocha Dealer","Cabana Dealer" / "Sorento Office","Mocha Office","Cabana Office"); "end user" → "End User"\n  - a TIER named as a "version" of a resource ("office version", "dealer version", "the office one", "give me the dealer copy") maps like the plain word: an access-level selection, NEVER a category/product/other entity, NEVER request_for_help', 'access_levels = the level(s) SELECTED or named IN THE CURRENT MESSAGE, ONLY from ["Sorento Dealer","Mocha Dealer","Mocha Office","Cabana Dealer","Cabana Office","End User","Sorento Office"]; never another string, an entity, carried forward or inferred; none → [].\n  - brand + "dealer" / "office" → that brand\'s level ("sorento" + "dealer" → "Sorento Dealer", "mocha" + "office" → "Mocha Office", the same for cabana); no brand → all three ("Sorento Dealer","Mocha Dealer","Cabana Dealer" / "Sorento Office","Mocha Office","Cabana Office"); "end user" → "End User"\n  - a TIER named as a "version" of a resource ("office version", "dealer version", "the office one", "give me the dealer copy") maps like the plain word: an access-level selection, NEVER a category/product/other entity, NEVER request_for_help'),
    # lever 4: terse.
    Edit('replace', 'An entity is a concrete, identifiable VALUE you could use to look up or filter a single record. Each hint means:', 'An entity = a concrete, identifiable VALUE that can look up or filter a single record. Each hint:'),
    # class 1 + lever 4: the attachment class list (catalogue | warranty | price tag template | 
    Edit('replace', "  - attachment → a named document resource from the company library. ALWAYS emit it, raw = the user's original words; canonical_code ONLY when the request clearly names one of these document classes — catalogue | warranty | price tag template | brand guarantee | container status — translating ANY language or synonym (katalog→catalogue; jaminan/waranti→warranty; senarai status kontena / container status report / container status sheet / shipping schedule→container status); for ANY other document null, never dropping the entity because no class fits.\n  - attachment_type → the KIND of document wanted, NAMED or IMPLIED (see ATTACHMENT TYPE EXTRACTION); canonical_code = the matching English kind the File type candidates block names, translating ANY language or synonym. EXCEPTION: authority/brand-named certificates (SPAN, SIRIM, BOMBA, MS####, Halal, Watermark/WCM/PPS) leave canonical_code null with the body name in raw. raw is always the user's original word.", "  - attachment → a named company-library document: ALWAYS emitted, raw = the user's words; canonical_code ONLY when it clearly names one of the attachment classes in the entity schema below, translating ANY language or synonym (katalog→catalogue; jaminan/waranti→warranty; senarai status kontena / container status report / container status sheet / shipping schedule→container status), else null.\n  - attachment_type → the KIND of document, NAMED or IMPLIED (ATTACHMENT TYPE EXTRACTION); canonical_code = the File type candidates kind in English, from ANY language or synonym, EXCEPT authority/brand-named certificates (SPAN, SIRIM, BOMBA, MS####, Halal, Watermark/WCM/PPS): canonical_code null, the body name in raw. raw = the user's own word."),
    # lever 4: the two lines merged; same three rules.
    Edit('replace', 'Extract the value even if unsure of its exact type, with your best-guess hint. Never absorb a filter value into user_goal only: if it can scope a lookup, it belongs in entities.\n\nIf there is no concrete identifiable value, entities = [].', 'Unsure of the exact type: extract it with your best-guess hint. A value that can scope a lookup belongs in entities, never only in user_goal; no concrete identifiable value → entities [].'),
    # lever 4: terse.
    Edit('replace', 'A GRAMMAR PARTICLE or filler word ("de", "lah", "ah", "leh", "loh", "the", "got", "的", "吗", "啊") is never an entity, in any language: "i want to see for srtwc286 de" -> entities [{"raw":"srtwc286","hint":"product"}] only ("de" is no warehouse).\nA BARE FAMILY CODE ("wc286", "7445", "kt1861", "srtwt": a short alphanumeric run like part of a product code), in any position and after any lead-in ("how about wc286"), is always {"raw":"<the token>","hint":"product"}, entity_op "replace_combine", never "reuse", never left out. With "purchase order" / "PO" it is message_type "business_query", never casual ("all wc286 purchase order" -> domain_hint "purchase_order", intent_hint "check_po").', 'A GRAMMAR PARTICLE or filler ("de", "lah", "ah", "leh", "loh", "the", "got", "的", "吗", "啊") is never an entity, any language: "i want to see for srtwc286 de" -> entities [{"raw":"srtwc286","hint":"product"}] only ("de" is no warehouse).\nA BARE FAMILY CODE ("wc286", "7445", "kt1861", "srtwt": a short alphanumeric run like part of a product code), anywhere and after any lead-in ("how about wc286"), is always {"raw":"<the token>","hint":"product"}, entity_op "replace_combine", never "reuse", never left out; with "purchase order" / "PO" it is message_type "business_query", never casual ("all wc286 purchase order" -> domain_hint "purchase_order", intent_hint "check_po").'),
    # class 1 + lever 4: replace_combine had two statements of what it replaces ("they REPLACE t
    Edit('replace', 'Each entity also carries a "confident" boolean:\n  - confident: true → a single clean referent: one word, a multi-word phrase naming ONE thing ("water closet", "<customer name>"), a part the USER labeled, or a lone code / single token EVEN IF you doubt it exists in the system. DEFAULT: when unsure, true.\n  - confident: false → ONLY when you had to cram MORE THAN ONE concept/type into one entity.raw because the user gave NO separation or label, so you cannot split it without guessing: "one <customer name> srtkt72ss" = quantity + a customer-ish name + a product code with no labels → ONE order entity, confident:false.\n  When the user DOES label the parts, SPLIT into separate entities, each confident:true:\n    "customer one <customer name>, product srtkt72ss"\n      → { "raw":"one <customer name>",  "hint":"customer", "confident":true }\n      → { "raw":"srtkt72ss", "hint":"product",  "confident":true }\n\nAlso emit ONE entity_op, how this turn relates to the previous entities:\n  - "clear" → the user broadened the ENTITY scope to everything with NO narrowing value ("show all promotions", "list everything"); entities = []. Widening ONE axis is NOT "clear" (see BROADEN AXIS).\n  - "replace_combine" → the user named one or more NEW scoping values (a new product, promotion, category, brand, customer, etc., even if it looks related to the old one): they REPLACE the previous scope; put them in entities.\n  - "replace" → "only X" / "just X" (in any language) when X is NOT the whole subject already on its own ("only TCNU3167091" over a subject that also carries a product, "just the SO" over one that also carries a customer): THIS MESSAGE\'s own entities become the WHOLE scope, every OTHER carried value dropped too. Unlike "replace_combine", where a plain new value REPLACES the axis it names and KEEPS every other carried axis (a new product still keeps the carried customer).\n  - "modify" → same subject as before, only an attribute changes ("the same product but its price instead"); entities = the unchanged subject, the change shows in domain/intent.\n  - "reuse" → no new scoping value, the SAME thing as before; downstream re-applies the previous entities unchanged.\n\nUnsure between replace_combine and reuse: a concrete new value → replace_combine, none → reuse.', '"confident" on each entity: true → one clean referent (a word; a multi-word phrase naming ONE thing: "water closet", "<customer name>"; a part the USER labeled; a lone code / token EVEN IF you doubt it exists), the DEFAULT when unsure; false → ONLY when you had to cram MORE THAN ONE concept/type into one entity.raw because the user gave NO separation or label ("one <customer name> srtkt72ss" = quantity + a customer-ish name + a product code → ONE order entity, confident:false). Labelled parts are SPLIT, each confident:true: "customer one <customer name>, product srtkt72ss" → customer "one <customer name>" + product "srtkt72ss"\n\nONE entity_op for how this turn relates to the previous entities:\n  - "clear" → the ENTITY scope broadened to everything, NO narrowing value ("show all promotions", "list everything"), entities []; widening ONE axis is NOT "clear" (BROADEN AXIS).\n  - "replace_combine" → one or more NEW scoping values (a new product, promotion, category, brand, customer, etc., even if related to the old one) in entities: each REPLACES the axis it names, every other carried axis KEPT (a new product keeps the carried customer).\n  - "replace" → "only X" / "just X" (any language) when X is NOT already the whole subject ("only TCNU3167091" over a subject that also carries a product, "just the SO" over one that also carries a customer): THIS MESSAGE\'s own entities become the WHOLE scope, every OTHER carried value dropped.\n  - "modify" → same subject, only an attribute changes ("the same product but its price instead"): entities = the unchanged subject, the change in domain/intent.\n  - "reuse" → no new scoping value, the SAME thing as before (downstream re-applies the previous entities).\nUnsure between replace_combine and reuse: a concrete new value → replace_combine, none → reuse.'),
    # class 1 + lever 4: the intro ("all time" drops the DATE filter, "all products" the PRODUCT
    Edit('replace', 'Users widen a question one axis at a time: "all time" drops the DATE filter, "all products" the PRODUCT filter; the rest of the question and its subject stay.\n\nbroaden_axis = the ONE axis widened this turn:\n  - "date": "all time", "any date", "all dates", "every date", "no date limit", "remove the date filter", "since ever", "not just August", in ANY phrasing or language, incl. a trailing emphatic particle ("...one", "...lah"). It widens the date FILTER of whatever is being asked; NEVER a shipment/ETA signal, NEVER moves domain_hint.\n  - an entity hint ("product", "customer", ..., the SAME hint name as for an entity of that kind): that filter is dropped, the enquiry unchanged: "all products", "any customer", "all transporters", "every warehouse".\n  - "all": everything broadened ("show me everything", "list all", no axis named); pair with entity_op "clear".\n  - null: nothing widened.\n\nbroaden_to = HOW FAR that axis is widened:\n  - "family": the one variant widened to EVERY VARIANT of its family, the family kept: "all variants of 286", "the whole 286 range", "every SRTWC286", "semua variant 286". Pair with broaden_axis "product".\n  - "all": the axis DROPPED entirely: "for all products", "any product", "all customers", "any customer", "any date", "all time", "okay nvm for all products".\n  - null: no widening; whenever broaden_axis is null, broaden_to is null too.\nbroaden_axis "all" with broaden_to "all" widens every axis at once ("show me everything"); the domain stays.\nOver a question scoped to SRTWC286-SH for <customer name>:\n  - "all variants of 286", "the whole 286 range" -> broaden_axis "product", broaden_to "family", entity_op "reuse", entities [] (the FAMILY WORD is not an entity here)\n  - "okay nvm for all products" / "for any products" -> broaden_axis "product", broaden_to "all", entities [], entity_op "reuse"\n\nWhen broaden_axis is "date" or an entity hint and a business domain is in play: KEEP the previous domain_hint and intent_hint ("all products" during an order enquiry is still an order enquiry; only ask-the-catalogue phrasing, "product list", "catalogue", "spec of X", moves it to master_products), scope_intent null, entity_op "reuse" (code drops the widened axis; never hand-prune entities).\nWith NO business domain in play, "all products" IS a catalogue request: domain_hint master_products, broaden_axis null.', 'broaden_axis = the ONE axis widened this turn (the rest of the question and its subject stay):\n  - "date": "all time", "any date", "all dates", "every date", "no date limit", "remove the date filter", "since ever", "not just August", ANY phrasing or language, incl. a trailing particle ("...one", "...lah"): the date FILTER of whatever is asked, NEVER a shipment/ETA signal, NEVER moves domain_hint.\n  - an entity hint ("product", "customer", ..., the SAME name as that entity\'s hint): that filter dropped, the enquiry unchanged: "all products", "any customer", "all transporters", "every warehouse".\n  - "all": everything broadened ("show me everything", "list all", no axis named), with broaden_to "all" and entity_op "clear"; the domain stays.\n  - null: nothing widened.\nbroaden_to = HOW FAR: "family" = one variant widened to EVERY VARIANT of its family, the family kept ("all variants of 286", "the whole 286 range", "every SRTWC286", "semua variant 286"), with broaden_axis "product", the FAMILY WORD no entity (entities []); "all" = the axis DROPPED ("for all products", "any product", "all customers", "any customer", "any date", "all time", "okay nvm for all products", "for any products"); null = no widening (always when broaden_axis is null).\nbroaden_axis "date" or an entity hint, business domain in play: KEEP the previous domain_hint and intent_hint ("all products" in an order enquiry stays an order enquiry; only ask-the-catalogue phrasing, "product list", "catalogue", "spec of X", moves to master_products), scope_intent null, entity_op "reuse" (code drops the widened axis; never hand-prune entities). NO business domain in play: "all products" IS a catalogue request, domain_hint master_products, broaden_axis null.'),
