    # lever 4: the two product_attachment rows on one line; "by meaning, any language" is the DE
    Edit('replace', 'Routing signals by meaning, any language (domain -> suggested_team / suggested_agent):\n  - master_products / product info -> "purchasing" / "general_enquiries"\n  - incoming -> "purchasing" / "incoming_stock_enquiries"\n  - product_attachment (photo/drawing/installation guide) -> "marketing_product" / "general_enquiries"\n  - product_attachment (certificate) -> "purchasing_certification" / "general_enquiries"\n  - forms -> "marketing_form" / "marketing_form"\n  - inventory / warehouse / stock -> "warehouse" / "general_enquiries"\n  - order -> "customer_service" / "order_enquiries"\n  - promotion -> "marketing_promotion" / "general_enquiries" (ONE team for every brand, never brand-suffixed)\n  - ideate (an idea is never escalated), or none of these this turn -> NO routing: null / null', 'Routing signals (domain -> suggested_team / suggested_agent):\n  - master_products / product info -> "purchasing" / "general_enquiries"\n  - incoming -> "purchasing" / "incoming_stock_enquiries"\n  - product_attachment: photo/drawing/installation guide -> "marketing_product" / "general_enquiries"; certificate -> "purchasing_certification" / "general_enquiries"\n  - forms -> "marketing_form" / "marketing_form"\n  - inventory / warehouse / stock -> "warehouse" / "general_enquiries"\n  - order -> "customer_service" / "order_enquiries"\n  - promotion -> "marketing_promotion" / "general_enquiries" (ONE team for every brand, never brand-suffixed)\n  - ideate, or none of these -> null / null'),
    # lever 4: "(order, promotion, incoming, anything)" restates "whatever the domain_hint"; the
    Edit('replace', '  date_filter_start / date_filter_end come ONLY from the CURRENT message: any date it names sets them, whatever the domain_hint (order, promotion, incoming, anything).\n  - ANY date, absolute or relative, PAST, PRESENT or FUTURE, made absolute from CURRENT DATE: "today", "yesterday", "last week", "this month"; "tomorrow" (= CURRENT DATE + 1 day), "next week", "next month", "in 3 days", a named weekday yet to come; "1 June", "May to June", "30/6". A single day is BOTH start and end ("tomorrow" on 29 June 2026 -> date_filter_start = "2026-06-30", date_filter_end = "2026-06-30").\n  - No date in the current message -> BOTH null, even if the previous turn or previous_conversation_state had one.\n  date_mode = HOW the window applies to a promotion\'s lifespan: ONLY when domain_hint = promotion AND a date filter is set this turn, else null.\n\ndate_mode by the VERB attached to the date, by meaning in any language:\n    - "started" -> RELEASED / LAUNCHED / STARTED / came out / is NEW within the window\n    - "ended" -> ENDED / EXPIRED / FINISHED / closed within the window\n    - "overlap" -> VALID / RUNNING / ACTIVE / available / ongoing during the window, or a date with no lifecycle verb ("promotions for June"); the default when unsure.', '  date_filter_start / date_filter_end ONLY from the CURRENT message: any date it names, whatever the domain_hint.\n  - ANY date, absolute or relative, PAST, PRESENT or FUTURE, made absolute from CURRENT DATE: "today", "yesterday", "last week", "this month"; "tomorrow" (= CURRENT DATE + 1 day), "next week", "next month", "in 3 days", a named weekday yet to come; "1 June", "May to June", "30/6". One day = BOTH start and end ("tomorrow" on 29 June 2026 -> date_filter_start = "2026-06-30", date_filter_end = "2026-06-30").\n  - No date in the current message -> BOTH null, even if the previous turn or previous_conversation_state had one.\n  date_mode = HOW the window applies to a promotion\'s lifespan, ONLY with domain_hint = promotion AND a date filter this turn, else null; by the VERB on the date, any language:\n    - "started" -> RELEASED / LAUNCHED / STARTED / came out / is NEW within the window\n    - "ended" -> ENDED / EXPIRED / FINISHED / closed within the window\n    - "overlap" -> VALID / RUNNING / ACTIVE / available / ongoing during the window, or no lifecycle verb ("promotions for June"); the default when unsure.'),
    # class 2 + lever 4: "the first two" → [1,2] dropped (same case as "the first three"). Every
    Edit('replace', 'If the user refers to items of the previous result set ("Previous response" may state N records) by POSITION, list each 1-based position in a top-level "reference_positions" array, never in entities, never inventing values: "the 3rd one" → [3]; "the last one" → [N]; "1st and 3rd", "2, 4 and 5" → [1,3] / [2,4,5]; "the first three", "1 to 3" → [1,2,3]; "the first two" → [1,2].\nA normal entity the user names (a product, category, customer) still goes in entities; both can be present. No positional reference → reference_positions = [].\nA BARE NUMBER, or one that only follows a lead-in word ("for", "number", "item") with nothing else naming it, no larger than the previous turn\'s record count is a POSITION, never a product/customer entity guess, even when some of those positions were answered on an earlier turn (the roster stays on screen until its own topic changes).\n  - Previous response listed 10 products; "okay how about stock, incoming and PO for 7" -> reference_positions [7], entities [] (never {"raw":"7","hint":"product"}).\nreference_positions is set ONLY when "Previous response" actually offered a numbered list: with no such list open, no number is a position.', 'Items of the previous result set ("Previous response" may state N records) referred to by POSITION -> each 1-based position in top-level "reference_positions", never in entities, never invented: "the 3rd one" → [3]; "the last one" → [N]; "1st and 3rd", "2, 4 and 5" → [1,3] / [2,4,5]; "the first three", "1 to 3" → [1,2,3]. A named entity (product, category, customer) still goes in entities, both may be present; none → [].\nA BARE NUMBER (or one after only a lead-in word: "for", "number", "item") no larger than the previous record count is a POSITION, never a product/customer guess, even when some of those positions were answered on an earlier turn: previous response listed 10 products, "okay how about stock, incoming and PO for 7" -> reference_positions [7], entities [] (never {"raw":"7","hint":"product"}). ONLY when "Previous response" actually offered a numbered list; with none open, no number is a position.'),
    # lever 4: arrow form; marker string and every example kept.
    Edit('replace', 'When "Previous response" contains the marker "[<N> did-you-mean suggestions active]" AND the current message refers to item position(s), also set a top-level "reference_target": "dym" when the reply is bare number(s) ("2", "1, 4", "1 and 4") or names a suggestion ("suggestion 2", "the 2nd suggestion"); "result" when it explicitly qualifies a result item ("product 2", "the 2nd one", "the 2nd product", "price of the first"). No marker → reference_target = null. reference_positions stays the raw 1-based positions; do NOT resolve them.', '"[<N> did-you-mean suggestions active]" in "Previous response" AND a positional reply -> also top-level "reference_target": "dym" for bare number(s) ("2", "1 and 4") or a named suggestion ("suggestion 2", "the 2nd suggestion"); "result" for a qualified result item ("product 2", "the 2nd one", "the 2nd product", "price of the first"). No marker -> reference_target = null. reference_positions stays the raw 1-based positions, never resolved.'),
