    Edit('replace', 'When the previous assistant message offered an escalation ("Would you like me to escalate ...") or asked which company to route to, a reply with a company name OR its short company code engages the pending offer, NOT a new business query: do not invent a domain_hint or entities from the company name/code alone.', 'After an offered escalation ("Would you like me to escalate ...") or a which-company-to-route-to question, a company name OR its short company code engages the pending offer, NOT a new business query: no domain_hint or entities from the name/code alone.'),
    # lever 4: terse, plus a pointer to the narrowed rule in ESCALATION CONFIRMATION; the "Compa
    Edit('replace', '  - If that list is NOT "(none)" AND the current message names EXACTLY ONE of those companies, by name OR code, bare or with confirmation/filler/request words around it ("Sorento team", "mocha please", "ok go with sorento", "route to mocha team", "yes please escalate to srt team", "please escalate to sorento team"), set "escalation": { "is_escalation_confirmation": true, "company_pick": "<the CANONICAL company name exactly as listed, e.g. Sorento — never the code>" }, whatever the message_type you assign (request_for_help, confirmation, casual). Do NOT set person_mention for a company name.\n  - Otherwise "company_pick" is null: no company named, a company NOT in the offered list ("yes mocha" when only Sorento is listed; the "yes" still counts as the affirmation), more than one named, or a negated company ("not sorento"). Never guess or resolve.\n  - A VALUE IS NOT A FRAGMENT. A concrete value you would extract as an entity (a customer/company NOT in the offered list, a product code, an order/DO/SPO number, a container, a warehouse) re-scopes the question as BARE ENTITY CONTINUATION says instead of answering the offer, with company_pick null and is_affirmative null: "for <customer name>" while a member picker is open is a customer filter, not a company pick and not small talk.\n  - Otherwise, a reply during a pending offer naming no company, no listed member, no value of its own, and not a yes/no (a bare fragment, small talk - but NOT the escalate word, which is a yes per AFFIRMATION/ESCALATE-WORD) is NOT a new business query and NOT a decline: casual/unknown, company_pick null, is_affirmative null, domain_hint null.', '  - That list NOT "(none)" AND the message IS the answer: EXACTLY ONE listed company, by name OR code, ALONE or with only confirmation, filler or request words ("mocha", "Mocha", "yes mocha", "the mocha one", "srt", "route to mch", "escalate to mocha team", "Sorento team", "mocha please", "ok go with sorento"), or the offered option\'s number, or a plain yes → "escalation": { "is_escalation_confirmation": true, "company_pick": "<the CANONICAL company name exactly as listed, e.g. Sorento — never the code>" }, whatever the message_type you assign (request_for_help, confirmation, casual). Do NOT set person_mention for a company name.\n  - Otherwise "company_pick" null: no company named, one NOT offered ("yes mocha" when only Sorento is listed; the "yes" still counts as the affirmation), more than one, or a negated one ("not sorento"). Never guess or resolve.\n  - A VALUE IS NOT A FRAGMENT. A concrete value you would extract as an entity (a customer/company NOT offered, a product code, an order/DO/SPO number, a container, a warehouse) re-scopes the question as BARE ENTITY CONTINUATION says, company_pick null, is_affirmative null: "for <customer name>" while a member picker is open is a customer filter, not a company pick and not small talk.\n  - Otherwise a reply naming no company, no listed member, no value of its own and no yes/no (a bare fragment, small talk; NOT the escalate word, a yes per AFFIRMATION/ESCALATE-WORD) is neither a new business query nor a decline: casual/unknown, company_pick null, is_affirmative null, domain_hint null.'),
