    # class 3: "answered by the outstanding report (sales_report is answered by the sales report
    Edit('replace', 'A STATUS VALUE MEANS THE ORDER DOMAIN: any "status" value ("outstanding", "so_outstanding", "do_outstanding", "outstanding_both", "delivered", "sales_report") is ORDER PAPER, answered by the outstanding report ("sales_report" is answered by the sales report instead; either way the domain is the same); NEVER domain_hint "inventory" with a status set. A document word -> that document\'s domain ("PO" -> purchase_order, "SPO" -> incoming); none named -> "order".', 'A STATUS VALUE MEANS THE ORDER DOMAIN: any "status" value ("outstanding", "so_outstanding", "do_outstanding", "outstanding_both", "delivered", "sales_report") is ORDER PAPER, NEVER domain_hint "inventory"; a document word -> that document\'s domain ("PO" -> purchase_order, "SPO" -> incoming), none named -> "order".'),
    # lever 4: the two examples inline; every misspelling and value kept.
    Edit('replace', '  - "Total outstanding SRTWC8518-SH" -> status "outstanding", document [], domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order" (NOT inventory / check_stock)\nREAD FOR MEANING, NOT SPELLING: a misspelt status word ("oustaning", "oustangind", "outstadning") or attribute word ("quantiyt", "quantiy") is still that word, never a fallback to domain_hint "inventory"; "dealer quantity" = "quantity"; "... report for <product>" beside a status word = "... quantity for <product>".\n  - "oustaning quantity for CB88SS" -> status "outstanding", domain_hint "order", requested_attributes ["quantity"]\n  - "how much stock for cb2805a" -> status null, domain_hint "inventory" (no status word)', '  - "Total outstanding SRTWC8518-SH" -> status "outstanding", document [], domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order" (NOT inventory / check_stock)\nREAD FOR MEANING, NOT SPELLING: a misspelt status word ("oustaning", "oustangind", "outstadning") or attribute word ("quantiyt", "quantiy") is still that word, never a fallback to "inventory"; "dealer quantity" = "quantity"; "... report for <product>" beside a status word = "... quantity for <product>": "oustaning quantity for CB88SS" -> status "outstanding", domain_hint "order", requested_attributes ["quantity"]; "how much stock for cb2805a" -> status null, domain_hint "inventory" (no status word).'),
    # class 1 + lever 4: "(a discontinued product, a promotion past its end date)" restates the 
    Edit('replace', 'is_active filters records by lifecycle status: ONLY from the CURRENT message\'s own words, by meaning in any language, never carried over.\n  - false -> INACTIVE/dead records: "discontinued", "expired", "ended", "obsolete", "no longer available", "old/past promotions", "delisted products" (a discontinued product, a promotion past its end date).\n  - true -> ACTIVE/current ones explicitly asked for: "active promotions", "current promos", "still available", "ongoing", "valid now".\n  - null -> DEFAULT, no lifecycle-status word: no status filter. A plain "show me Sorento promotions" -> null, NOT true.', 'is_active, ONLY from the CURRENT message\'s own words (by meaning, any language), never carried over: false -> INACTIVE/dead records ("discontinued", "expired", "ended", "obsolete", "no longer available", "old/past promotions", "delisted products"); true -> ACTIVE/current ones explicitly asked for ("active promotions", "current promos", "still available", "ongoing", "valid now"); null -> DEFAULT, no lifecycle-status word ("show me Sorento promotions" -> null, NOT true).'),
    # lever 4: the six mapping rows on one line, examples inline; every code, word and value kep
    Edit('replace', '"document" = WHICH KIND OF PAPER the message is about, codes from this closed set only: "SO" (sales order), "DO" (delivery order), "PO" (purchase order), "SPO" (supplier purchase order / shipment), "GRN" (goods receive note). From the CURRENT message\'s own words, any language, never carried over; default [] (no paper named).\n  - "sales order", "SO", "sales orders" -> ["SO"]\n  - "delivery order", "DO", "delivery orders", "DO list" -> ["DO"]\n  - "purchase order", "PO" -> ["PO"]\n  - "SPO", "shipment", "container" -> ["SPO"]\n  - "GRN", "goods receive", "goods received note" -> ["GRN"]\n  - "both", "SO and DO", "sales order and delivery order" -> ["SO", "DO"]\nTHE DOCUMENT WORD COUNTS WHEREVER IT SITS IN THE MESSAGE - before the status word, after it, beside the product, in the middle of a long sentence, and through a typo in a NEIGHBOURING word (location examples with their order_status under ORDER_STATUS GAINS "do_outstanding" below).\n  - "Outstsnding DO for 7445" -> document ["DO"], status "outstanding" (the typo is in the status word, not the document word)\nA message that is ONLY a paper word is still that paper, and it is a business_query -\nnever casual, never an empty document.\n  - "Sales order" -> document ["SO"], message_type "business_query", domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order"\n  - "can show both?" (over an outstanding SO/DO detail offer) -> document ["SO", "DO"], status "outstanding", reference_positions [] ("both" there names BOTH PAPERS, not a position off the list).', '"document" = WHICH KIND OF PAPER, codes from this closed set only: "SO" (sales order), "DO" (delivery order), "PO" (purchase order), "SPO" (supplier purchase order / shipment), "GRN" (goods receive note); from the CURRENT message\'s own words, any language, never carried over; default [].\n  - "sales order", "SO", "sales orders" -> ["SO"]; "delivery order", "DO", "delivery orders", "DO list" -> ["DO"]; "purchase order", "PO" -> ["PO"]; "SPO", "shipment", "container" -> ["SPO"]; "GRN", "goods receive", "goods received note" -> ["GRN"]; "both", "SO and DO", "sales order and delivery order" -> ["SO", "DO"]\nTHE DOCUMENT WORD COUNTS WHEREVER IT SITS (before or after the status word, beside the product, mid-sentence, through a typo in a NEIGHBOURING word; location examples under ORDER_STATUS GAINS "do_outstanding"): "Outstsnding DO for 7445" -> document ["DO"], status "outstanding".\nONLY a paper word is still that paper and a business_query, never casual, never an empty document: "Sales order" -> document ["SO"], message_type "business_query", domain_hint "order", intent_hint "check_order"; "can show both?" (over an outstanding SO/DO detail offer) -> document ["SO", "DO"], status "outstanding", reference_positions [] ("both" names BOTH PAPERS there, not a position).'),
    # lever 4: terse; same rule and example.
    Edit('replace', '"asks" = EVERY domain the CURRENT message asks about, in its order, as {"domain": "<domain name>", "intent": "<intent_hint for that domain, or null>"}, domain names from the domain block at the end of this prompt. domain_hint stays the FIRST of them.\nOne domain or none -> "asks": null. Only THIS message\'s words: never a second domain from the previous turn, the current subject, or what the answer might usefully include.\n"also", "as well", "too" ADD the new domain to the standing one: asks with the STANDING domain first, the new one second, never the new one alone ("i want stock also" right after an order question -> order first, then inventory; domain_hint "order").', '"asks" = EVERY domain the CURRENT message asks about, in order, as {"domain": "<domain name>", "intent": "<intent_hint for that domain, or null>"} (domain names from the domain block at the end of this prompt); domain_hint = the FIRST. One domain or none -> "asks": null. Only THIS message\'s words, never a domain from the previous turn, the current subject, or what the answer might usefully include. "also", "as well", "too" ADD the new domain after the STANDING one, never alone ("i want stock also" right after an order question -> order, then inventory; domain_hint "order").'),
    # lever 4: terse. Pass 4: tighter.
    Edit('replace', '"topic_reset" is true when the message DROPS the conversation\'s subject for something else ("never mind", "forget that", "different question", "ok now promotions"). Judged by SUBJECT, not wording: a refinement, a narrower filter, a pick off a list and a follow-up question stay false. Default false.', '"topic_reset" = true when the message DROPS the subject for something else ("never mind", "forget that", "different question", "ok now promotions"); judged by SUBJECT: a refinement, a narrower filter, a pick off a list or a follow-up question stays false (the default).'),
